python -m pip install faiss-cpu



| Package / Tool            | Used In                      | Purpose                         |
| ------------------------- | ---------------------------- | ------------------------------- |
| Python                    | Entire project               | Runtime                         |
| FastAPI                   | `app.py`, `api/`             | Backend REST API                |
| Uvicorn                   | Server                       | Run FastAPI                     |
| Streamlit                 | `streamlit_app.py`           | Frontend UI                     |
| LangChain                 | Multiple modules             | RAG framework                   |
| langchain-community       | `loaders/`, `vectorstore/`   | PDF loaders, FAISS, CSV loader  |
| langchain-text-splitters  | `chunking/splitter.py`       | Split documents                 |
| langchain-ollama          | `models/`, `embeddings/`     | Connect to Ollama               |
| Ollama (tool)             | Local machine                | Runs LLM and embedding models   |
| `ollama` (Python package) | Optional                     | Direct Python API to Ollama     |
| FAISS                     | `vectorstore/faiss_store.py` | Store and search vectors        |
| ChromaDB                  | Future alternative           | Vector database                 |
| pypdf                     | `loaders/pdf_loader.py`      | Read PDF files                  |
| python-docx               | `loaders/docx_loader.py`     | Read DOCX files                 |
| pandas                    | `loaders/csv_loader.py`      | Read CSV files                  |
| NumPy                     | FAISS, embeddings            | Numerical arrays                |
| PostgreSQL                | Future                       | Store chat history and metadata |
| psycopg2-binary           | Database layer               | PostgreSQL driver               |
| SQLAlchemy                | Database layer               | ORM                             |
| Redis                     | Future                       | Cache and sessions              |
| python-dotenv             | `config/settings.py`         | Load `.env` values              |
| pydantic                  | API models                   | Validate requests/responses     |
| pydantic-settings         | `config/settings.py`         | Manage application settings     |
| python-multipart          | Upload API                   | Handle file uploads             |
| httpx                     | Future services              | HTTP client                     |
| tiktoken                  | Future prompt management     | Token counting                  |
| pytest                    | `tests/`                     | Unit and integration testing    |



python -m pip install fastapi uvicorn streamlit langchain langchain-core langchain-community langchain-text-splitters langchain-ollama ollama faiss-cpu chromadb sentence-transformers pypdf python-docx beautifulsoup4 lxml pandas numpy redis sqlalchemy psycopg2-binary python-dotenv python-multipart httpx requests tiktoken pytest pydantic pydantic-settings


install ollama on your local machine from the official website:

https://ollama.com/download?utm_source=chatgpt.com

Step 2: Install
Double-click the downloaded .exe file.
Click Next until the installation finishes.
Ollama will install as a Windows service.
Step 3: Verify Installation

Open Command Prompt, PowerShell, or Git Bash and run:

ollama --version

Step 4: Start Ollama

Normally, Ollama starts automatically.

If needed, run:

ollama serve

Step 5: Download Models

Download the LLM:

ollama pull llama3.2

Download the embedding model:

ollama pull nomic-embed-text

Step 7: Test the LLM
ollama run llama3.2

Step 8: Test the API

Open your browser:

http://localhost:11434

or use:

curl http://localhost:11434/api/tags